            "review_title": "Review at 5Ku Quan Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Arnewoodian\nNew Forest National Park Hampshire, United Kingdom58 contributions\n0\nMuch better than it looks from the outside\nApr 2019 • Solo\nThis place is on a street corner and open on both sides, it is cavernous and looks like a cattle shed with corrugated roofing. But what had attracted me was the large area of fishtanks where the live seafood was kept. There were long rows of tables and chairs all lined up as if for some giant feast, I was very early and so there was only one other group of diners at the start. The staff were very apologetic explaining that as it was so early the BBQ was not yet fired up, so some of the menu was unavailable. However I settled for grilled tiger prawns, and beef with chili and lemongrass, along with several bottles of Larue, the local beer. Despite the inauspicious start and no frills appearance, this was a really delicious dinner and excellent value at just 288,000 Dong including drinks. If I was in the city for longer I would have been back for more.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 27, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
